ng it Lean Republican and one Solid Republican. Available polls are hypothetical and show Begich's first-choice support in the mid-40s to low-50s, short of a majority, which keeps ranked-choice dynamics in play. A prediction market prices Democratic chances near three percent. The race remains Begich's to lose, with the independent's appeal to anti-incumbent voters the main source of uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1234, "margin": -7.11}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1042, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0943, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1159, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0428, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0916, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1248, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0896, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0885, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.063, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1006, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0993, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1268, "margin": -7.5}]}